Q1. What is the Builder Design Pattern?
Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

The Builder Pattern is a
Creational Design Pattern
used to construct complex
objects step by step.

It separates the construction
process from the final object,
making object creation more
flexible and readable.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need Builder Pattern?

• Solves the Telescoping Constructor Problem.
• Handles objects with many fields.
• Supports Optional Parameters.
• Improves Readability.
• Improves Maintainability.
• Prevents confusion in constructor arguments.

------------------------------------------------------------

When should we use it?

Use Builder Pattern when

• A class has many fields.
• Many fields are optional.
• Constructors become too long.
• Constructor overloading becomes difficult.

------------------------------------------------------------

Real-Life Example

Making Tea

Water

↓

Tea Leaves

↓

Sugar

↓

Milk

↓

Tea Ready

Tea is prepared
step by step.

------------------------------------------------------------

Software Industry Example

User user = User.builder()

        .setName("Vishal")

        .setAge(22)

        .setEmail("vishal@gmail.com")

        .build();

