Q2. How does Builder Pattern solve the
Telescoping Constructor Problem?

Interview Ready Answer

Telescoping Constructor Problem

When a class contains many fields,

multiple overloaded constructors
are created.

Example

Student()

Student(String name)

Student(String name,int age)

Student(String name,int age,
String email)

Student(String name,int age,
String email,String address)

As fields increase,

constructors also increase,

making the code difficult
to understand and maintain.

------------------------------------------------------------

Builder Solution

Instead of remembering the
order of constructor parameters,

use Builder.

Student student = Student.builder()

        .setName("Vishal")

        .setAge(22)

        .setEmail("vishal@gmail.com")

        .setAddress("Agra")

        .build();

------------------------------------------------------------

Benefits

• No need to remember
  parameter order.

• Better Readability.

• Better Maintainability.

• Supports Optional Fields.

• Reduces Constructor Overloading.

------------------------------------------------------------

Memory Trick

Many Fields

↓

Many Constructors

↓

Telescoping Constructor Problem

↓

Builder Pattern

↓

Step-by-Step Object Construction

