Q3. Difference between Factory Method
and Builder Pattern

Interview Ready Answer

Factory Method Pattern

• Creates objects without exposing
  the concrete class.

• Solves

  "Which object should be created?"

• Returns different object types.

• Hides Object Creation Logic.

Example

Vehicle vehicle =
VehicleFactory.getVehicle("Car");

------------------------------------------------------------

Builder Pattern

• Builds complex objects
  step by step.

• Solves

  "How should the object be built?"

• Usually constructs one
  complex object.

• Hides Object Construction Logic.

Example

Student student = Student.builder()

        .setName("Vishal")

        .setAge(22)

        .setEmail("vishal@gmail.com")

        .build();

------------------------------------------------------------

Memory Trick

Factory

↓

WHICH Object?

↓

Car

Bike

Truck

----------------------------

Builder

↓

HOW to Build?

↓

Name

↓

Age

↓

Email

↓

Build()

